    "reasoning": "All 16 numerical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. However, q-51405 contains authored errors: the central-difference formula uses g instead of v, and the calculation and conclusion incorrectly label the requested time t=3 as t=2. The actual computation [v(4)-v(2)]/2=(3-1)/2=1 correctly answers the question at t=3. The remaining mathematics checks out: normal symmetry gives 0.0104, 1-0.7673=0.2327, and 1-2(0.4286)=0.1428. Using the source's geometric convention X=1,2,... gives 0.15(0.85)^6≈0.0566; 0.4(0.6)^4≈0.0518; 1-(0.85)^2=0.2775; (0.77)^3-(0.77)^6≈0.2481; (1/3)^5≈0.0041; and (2/5)^4=0.0256. The tangent zero at x=π/3 gives C=-π/5. The cotangent asymptotes and midpoint give B=3 and D=1, hence B+D=4. The application probabilities are (0.75)^3(0.25)≈0.105 and 1-(0.5)^5≈0.969. For the rocket, y=4 and y'=zz'/y=1250 km/h. Integrating the acceleration gives v(t)=⟨sin(3t),cos(t)-1/2⟩, whose only zero in the stated interval is t=π/3. No submitted grades or earlier answers are supplied; the MA evidence below comes exclusively from each question's own worked solution.",
